$DIR/main.p:5:34: float64 constant is not allowed in kernel mode (no FPU state is saved; mark the function //pu:fpu to use floats)
    The function scale uses floating point here (float64 constant), and this is
    a kernel-mode build, where only functions marked //pu:fpu may use floating
    point. When an interrupt or system call enters the kernel, the processor
    does not save the floating-point registers, so kernel code that used them
    would corrupt the values of the program it interrupted.
    Copying a struct with float fields is allowed, since that uses only integer
    registers.
    Go has no kernel mode. Plutonium rejects floats here, rather than emulate
    them in software, so that no hidden cost or library ends up in the kernel.
    Mark the function, and have its callers save the floating-point state with
    x86.FPUBegin and x86.FPUEnd:
        //pu:fpu
        func scale(...)
    (see "Floating point in kernel mode" in the Plutonium spec, section 11.3)
    (run "pluto explain E2520" for a longer explanation)
